# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE suppression list
#
# Governance policy (enforced by scripts/check-trivyignore.sh and CI):
#   1. Every entry MUST include an exp:YYYY-MM-DD expiry date (typically 90 days).
#   2. Every entry MUST have a comment block above it explaining why it's suppressed.
#   3. Every comment block MUST include a link (https://) to the upstream issue.
#
# When a suppression nears expiry, re-evaluate:
#   - If a fix is available: update the image/chart version and remove the entry.
#   - If no fix yet: renew with a new expiry date and update the comment.
#
# Run locally: scripts/check-trivyignore.sh

# OpenSSL high-severity vulnerability in Debian base of Authentik image
# (ghcr.io/goauthentik/server:2026.2.1). No patched image available yet;
# waiting for Debian to publish openssl 3.5.4-1~deb13u2 and Authentik to
# rebuild their image from the updated base.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-15467
CVE-2025-15467 exp:2026-09-29

# Go crypto/tls session resumption issue affecting the Go runtime bundled in
# several images. Fixed in Go 1.24.13/1.25.7, but upstream images have not
# yet published a rebuild based on the patched Go toolchain.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-09-29

# Go html/template vulnerabilities in the Redis Alpine image, which bundles
# an older Go binary (v1.18). Fixed in Go 1.19.8+/1.20.3+, but the Redis
# Docker image has not yet been rebuilt with a patched Go runtime.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-24538
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-24540
CVE-2023-24538 exp:2026-09-29
CVE-2023-24540 exp:2026-09-29

# Go net/netip issue in the Redis Alpine image (old Go v1.18 runtime).
# Fixed in Go 1.21.11+/1.22.4+; waiting for the Redis image to be rebuilt.
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24790
CVE-2024-24790 exp:2026-09-29
